{"study_accession":"PRJNA893903","secondary_study_accession":"SRP404336","title":"Autosomal recessive PIK3CD deficiency","description":"We studied a case with suspected PIK3CD deficiency with a homozygous mutation in the patient in PIK3CD (c.1340-1 G>A). All other family members were tested and defined as carriers of the same mutation and are clinically healthy. The literature states that there is an AD but also an AR form of the disease  (Immunodeficiency 14 A and B, respectively) linked to the gene. The clinical phenotype of the patient fits very well the description as LOF she suffers from severe, recurrent infections since infancy and has low overall IgG levels. Overall design: We studied a case with suspected PIK3CD deficiency with a homozygous mutation in the patient in PIK3CD (c.1340-1 G>A). Whole peripheral blood was preserved in Tempus solution and RNA was extracted according to the standard protocol.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":3,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN31436862","study_accession":"PRJNA893903","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"091-P18","description":"091-P18","sex":"female","geo_sample":"GSM6674913","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2024-01-01","attributes":[["source_name","peripheral blood"],["individual","Patient"],["sex","female"],["tissue","peripheral blood"],["cell_type","PBMCs"],["genotype","c.1340-1 G>A/c.1340-1 G>A"],["disease","PIK3CD deficiency"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR22029775","experiment_accession":"SRX18011033","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":151183145,"base_count":45657309790,"first_public":"2024-01-01","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM6674913: 091-P18 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN31436863","study_accession":"PRJNA893903","blood_class":"pbmc","cla